{"kind":"request","text":"Planner: decide the scope of declared acts stage 5's UI entry (request a5d64b35). This owes a decision only: no Git artifact, no landing.\n\nThe checker's stage 5 review 0b33e8cc, item 3, finds that condition 1 (\"a UI that renders declared labels and typed fields and can prepare and submit an application act\") and condition 3 (\"show it in CLI and UI\") are not met in full: the generic form and the LiveRoom adapter exist and are tested against the memory room, but packages/ui/src/main.tsx selects only the memory room or the mock room, so no authenticated entry reaches a real Room. It asks me to complete that integration through the existing client, credential and surface owners, or to obtain an explicit requester scope decision. It adds no login or room-selection design and no first-Jam gate.\n\nThe facts. The UI has no way today for a person to hold a credential in the browser: there is no login, no key custody and no room selection in packages/ui. Those are commissioned as the connected-story work packages: 18815307 (browser identity, onboarding and authorized import, package 4) and cfbde32f (the browser task, progress, steering and review journey, package 5), both open and not yet promised. Wiring the Acts page to a live room needs exactly what package 4 delivers. Building a second, smaller credential path inside stage 5 would duplicate it and would be the unreviewed login design the checker says it is not asking for.\n\nThe options I see. (1) Stage 5's UI entry is delivered when package 4 gives the browser a credential: the Acts page's live entry and its real-Room witness move to 18815307 or cfbde32f, named there as an acceptance item, and stage 5 is reviewed for the rest. (2) Stage 5 keeps it, and waits for package 4. (3) Stage 5 adds a development-only entry: a URL that takes a room and a bearer token typed by the person, with one real-Room test. That is small, but it puts a token in a page with no custody design.\n\nMy recommendation is (1). The two other stage 5 findings of 0b33e8cc, the capacity reservation and the pending intent across a catalogue failure, are being repaired now under stage 5.","body":{"conditions":"(1) A decision, with reasons: whether the authenticated UI entry stays in stage 5's scope or moves to a named request, and which. (2) If it moves: the acceptance item is written into that request, and stage 5's review is told which of conditions 1 and 3 it still binds. (3) If it stays: what counts as the authenticated entry and its witness.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}